==================================================
16. NAMING

Use semantic names.

GOOD:

empty-organize.svg
achievement-early-bird.svg
battle-seven-to-smoke.svg
decorative-bracket-grid.svg

BAD:

asset1.svg
image-new.svg
vector-final2.svg
shape.svg

==================================================
17. SVG OPTIMIZATION

SVG output must be production ready.

Avoid:

thousands of unnecessary path nodes
base64 raster images inside SVG
embedded fonts
unused defs
duplicate gradients
massive filter regions
invisible geometry
editor metadata

Keep paths reasonably simple.

Prefer reusable groups and defs.

Use:

<defs>
<linearGradient>
<radialGradient>
<filter>
<clipPath>
<mask>

where they improve maintainability.

==================================================
18. ACCESSIBILITY

Decorative SVG:

aria-hidden="true"

Meaningful SVG:

role="img"
aria-labelledby

Do not duplicate text read by screen readers if the adjacent HTML already communicates the meaning.

==================================================
19. REACT USAGE

For illustrations stored in public:

<img
  src="/bynd8/illustrations/empty/organize.svg"
  alt=""
  aria-hidden="true"
/>

For interactive/currentColor icons:

prefer React SVG components or the existing icon system.

Do not paste a 200-line SVG directly into page components.

==================================================
20. EMPTY STATE COMPONENT

Use a shared application component such as:

<DancerEmptyState
  artwork="/bynd8/illustrations/empty/organize.svg"
  title="Got an event in mind?"
  description="Create your first event and bring the scene together."
  primaryAction={...}
/>

The illustration provides visual storytelling.

The component provides layout.

Do not duplicate entire empty-state layouts per page.

==================================================
21. VISUAL QA

Every new illustration must be previewed against the actual BYND8 background:

#080908

Never review an SVG only against a white browser/file preview.

Test it at:

390px
768px
1024px
1440px
1920px

Check:

- silhouette readability
- no white rectangle
- no fake checkerboard
- no clipping
- no stretched artwork
- no unreadable decorative text
- no excessive glow
- no tiny details dominating file size
- no broken gradients
- no unexpected background

==================================================
22. BEFORE CREATING AN SVG

Always inspect:

1. Existing BYND8 visual references.
2. Existing related assets.
3. Existing design tokens.
4. Intended screen and dimensions.
5. Whether SVG is actually the correct medium.

Then briefly define:

PURPOSE
VISUAL METAPHOR
PRIMARY SUBJECT
ENVIRONMENT
ACCENT COLOR
RESPONSIVE BEHAVIOR

before creating the asset.

==================================================
23. AFTER CREATING AN SVG

Do not assume valid XML means good artwork.

Render it.

Open the actual page.

Compare it against the supplied visual reference.

If it looks like generic developer art, redesign it.

Visual quality matters as much as technical validity.

==================================================
24. DO NOT MODIFY PRODUCT BEHAVIOR

Creating/replacing artwork must not change:

authentication
navigation
event logic
registration
payment
organizer behavior
competition behavior

SVG work is visual unless the task explicitly says otherwise.